# Landmine instance segmentation (YOLO11s-seg, models/landmine.onnx, 1 class: "landmine").
#
# Deliberately NOT DetectObjects.srv. That service returns bounding boxes only, and a box is
# not enough here: the grasp needs the DETONATOR located to a couple of millimetres and its
# YAW recovered (a 45 deg yaw error is a corner grasp). A box gives neither. The mask does.
#
# The model finds the WHOLE MINE (disc + detonator), not the detonator alone -- its one class
# is "landmine". So the mask is the region of interest, and the detonator is localised inside
# it (see grasp_mtc/scripts/landmine_detector.py). That split is the point: the learned model
# does the robust "is there a mine, and where", and the geometry does the precise "where
# exactly do I put the jaws".
sensor_msgs/Image image
---
# One entry per detected mine, ranked by confidence.
mobile_manipulator/Detection[] detections

# One mask per detection, SAME INDEX as detections[], mono8, SAME SIZE AS THE REQUEST IMAGE
# (the network runs at 960x960; these are already scaled back). 255 = mine, 0 = not.
sensor_msgs/Image[] masks

sensor_msgs/Image annotated_image
float32 inference_time_ms
